docs/remote-client.md:131:  - at most 16 connections in total and 4 unauthenticated ones; a further accept is closed at once. The 4 are a separate pool: an unauthenticated flood fills its own slots and never a paired client's. A request for one of the web page's files (`GET /`, `/app.js`, `/app.css`) is an unauthenticated connection like any other: it counts in the pool from accept, is answered on the connection thread from the embedded bytes without reaching the frame, and its reply carries `Connection: close`, so a load frees its slot at once rather than holding it for the idle timeout (Spike 23 measured four of five parallel page requests served against the pool);
